Ignore-case policy operators only fold ASCII
Link: https://chatgpt.com/codex/cloud/security/findings/4f47fd77fb3081918ffc397a4fca11e6?repo=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fjustincormack%2Fargmin&sev=
Criticality: medium (attack path: medium)
Status: fixed

# Resolution
Reviewed against AWS on 03/05/2026. The finding is valid: AWS
`StringEqualsIgnoreCase` and `StringNotEqualsIgnoreCase` match non-ASCII UTF-8
case variants such as `sëcret` and `SËCRET` in request object tag values, while
the local evaluator previously used Rust `eq_ignore_ascii_case` and only folded
ASCII.

Fixed in commit `1b1d8d5` (`Match S3 ignore-case Unicode policy matching`) by
changing the ignore-case string condition operators to compare Unicode lowercase
forms rather than ASCII-only case folding. Added auth unit coverage and
AWS-facing s3-tests for both positive and negative operators:

- `string_equals_ignore_case_matches_non_ascii_case_variants`
- `string_not_equals_ignore_case_rejects_non_ascii_case_variants`
- `test_bucket_policy_string_equals_ignore_case_request_object_tag_non_ascii`
- `test_bucket_policy_string_not_equals_ignore_case_request_object_tag_non_ascii`

Validation:

- `cargo test -p auth non_ascii_case_variants -- --nocapture`
- `cargo nextest run -p s3-tests --test bucket_policy test_bucket_policy_string_equals_ignore_case_request_object_tag_non_ascii test_bucket_policy_string_not_equals_ignore_case_request_object_tag_non_ascii`
- `./scripts/aws-tests --test bucket_policy test_bucket_policy_string_equals_ignore_case_request_object_tag_non_ascii -- --nocapture`
- `./scripts/aws-tests --test bucket_policy test_bucket_policy_string_not_equals_ignore_case_request_object_tag_non_ascii -- --nocapture`
- `cargo clippy -p auth -p s3-tests --tests -- -D warnings`

